Working title: RogueBreaker
Engine: Unity/C#
Target Platform: WebGL/Windows on Itch.io

Core Game Loop & Run Rules
1. Wave Initialization:
  A structured pattern of destructible bricks spawns.
  Player spawns with 3 lives for that wave.
  Player starts with a baseline allowance of 1 dash charge per wave (expandable/rechargeable via upgrades).
2. Action Phase (Breakout + QTE):
  The ball bounces between boundary walls, the paddle, and brick layouts.
  Base Dash: Triggered on demand to reposition rapidly across the board. Reacts to cursor position.
  QTE Movement Trigger: When specific events occur (e.g., ball entering a defined "Danger Zone" near the bottom gutter or an incoming projectile hazard), a brief, non-intrusive prompt appears (e.g., timed button strike or micro-directional flick) that rewards the player with an instantaneous dash, extended reach, or a trajectory redirection.
3. Wave Completion & Drafting:
  Clearing all target bricks halts gameplay and presents an upgrade selection screen.
  Player drafts 1 of 3 randomized perks/modifiers.
4. Escalation & Boss Phase:
  Stages 1 to 5 escalate brick density, movement speed, and hazard frequency.
5. Permadeath & Failure:
  Losing all 3 lives during any wave ends the run immediately.

